{"id":"mahabharata-13-075","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":75,"title":"पञ्चसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 75 · The rule of giving cows","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks for the rule of giving cows, so that he and his brothers might win the eternal worlds. Bhishma gives the prayers a giver should say, and tells of the king Saudasa, who gave cows to the sages and obtained the worlds he wished, and so the king never yoked a cow to his pole.","kn":"ನಿತ್ಯ ಲೋಕ ಪಡೆಯಲು ಗೋದಾನದ ವಿಧಿ ಹೇಳಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದಾತ ಹೇಳಬೇಕಾದ ಪ್ರಾರ್ಥನೆಗಳನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳಿ ಋಷಿಗಳಿಗೆ ಗೋವು ನೀಡಿ ಬಯಸಿದ ಲೋಕ ಪಡೆದ ರಾಜ ಸೌದಾಸನ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर गोदान का विधान पूछते हैं ताकि वे और उनके भाई शाश्वत लोक पाएँ। भीष्म दाता द्वारा बोली जाने वाली प्रार्थनाएँ बताते हैं और राजा सौदास की कथा कहते हैं जिसने ऋषियों को गौएँ देकर इच्छित लोक पाए।","te":"తాను, తన తమ్ములు శాశ్వత లోకాలను పొందేలా గోదాన విధిని చెప్పమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. దాత చెప్పవలసిన ప్రార్థనలను భీష్ముడు చెప్పి, ఋషులకు ఆవులిచ్చి కోరిన లోకాలు పొందిన రాజు సౌదాసుని కథ చెబుతాడు.","ta":"தாமும் தம் சகோதரரும் நிலையான உலகங்களைப் பெறும்படி பசுதான விதியைக் கூறுமாறு யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, கொடையாளி கூற வேண்டிய வேண்டுதல்களைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறி, முனிவர்களுக்குப் பசுக்களைத் தந்து விரும்பிய உலகங்களைப் பெற்ற மன்னன் சௌதாசனின் கதையைக் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"പശുദാനത്തിന്റെ നിയമം പറയണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; താനും സഹോദരന്മാരും ശാശ്വത ലോകങ്ങൾ നേടേണ്ടതിനാണിത്. ദാതാവ് ചൊല്ലേണ്ട പ്രാർത്ഥനകൾ ഭീഷ്മർ നൽകുന്നു; മുനിമാർക്ക് പശുക്കളെ ദാനം ചെയ്ത് താൻ ആഗ്രഹിച്ച ലോകങ്ങൾ നേടിയ സൗദാസ രാജാവിന്റെ കഥയും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. അതിനുശേഷം ആ രാജാവ് ഒരിക്കലും പശുവിനെ തന്റെ രഥത്തിൽ നുകം വെച്ചു കെട്ടിയില്ല."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.75; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विधिं गवां परमहं श्रोतुमिच्छामि तत्त्वतः ।\nयेन ताञ्शाश्वताँल्लोकानखिलानश्नुवीमहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to hear the true rule for giving cows, by which we may win the eternal worlds in full."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"न गोदानात्परं किंचिद्विद्यते वसुधाधिप ।\nगौर्हि न्यायागता दत्ता सद्यस्तारयते कुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O lord of the earth, nothing is greater than the gift of a cow. A cow rightly obtained and given at once lifts one's whole family across."}},{"n":3,"text":"सतामर्थे सम्यगुत्पादितो यः\nस वै कॢप्तः सम्यगिष्टः प्रजाभ्यः ।\nतस्मात्पूर्वं ह्यादिकाले प्रवृत्तं\nगवां दाने शृणु राजन्विधिं मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"What was properly produced for the good and offered well for the sake of creatures is established. So, O king, hear from me the rule for giving cows that began in the first age."}},{"n":4,"text":"पुरा गोषूपनीतासु गोषु संदिग्धदर्शिना ।\nमान्धात्रा प्रकृतं प्रश्नं बृहस्पतिरभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, when cows were being brought forward, Mandhata, unsure of the matter, put the question, and Brihaspati answered it."}},{"n":5,"text":"द्विजातिमभिसत्कृत्य श्वः कालमभिवेद्य च ।\nप्रदानार्थे नियुञ्जीत रोहिणीं नियतव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having honoured a brahmin and told him the time for the next day, the giver, firm in his vow, should set apart a Rohini cow for the gift."}},{"n":6,"text":"आह्वानं च प्रयुञ्जीत समङ्गे बहुलेति च ।\nप्रविश्य च गवां मध्यमिमां श्रुतिमुदाहरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should call out, 'Samanga!' and 'Bahula!', and entering among the cows should recite this sacred text."}},{"n":7,"text":"गौर्मे माता गोवृषभः पिता मे\nदिवं शर्म जगती मे प्रतिष्ठा ।\nप्रपद्यैवं शर्वरीमुष्य गोषु\nमुनिर्वाणीमुत्सृजेद्गोप्रदाने ॥","meaning":{"en":"'The cow is my mother, the bull my father; they are heaven, my shelter, and the world's foundation.' Having spent the night with the cows after saying this, the sage should utter these words at the giving of the cow."}},{"n":8,"text":"स तामेकां निशां गोभिः समसख्यः समव्रतः ।\nऐकात्म्यगमनात्सद्यः कल्मषाद्विप्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For that one night he lives among the cows as their equal, keeping their way of life, and by becoming one with them he is quickly freed from sin."}},{"n":9,"text":"उत्सृष्टवृषवत्सा हि प्रदेया सूर्यदर्शने ।\nत्रिविधं प्रतिपत्तव्यमर्थवादाशिषः स्तवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The cow, with the bull and calf released, should be given at sunrise. Three kinds of utterance are to be understood: explanatory praise, blessings, and hymns."}},{"n":10,"text":"ऊर्जस्विन्य ऊर्जमेधाश्च यज्ञो\nगर्भोऽमृतस्य जगतश्च प्रतिष्ठा ।\nक्षितौ राधःप्रभवः शश्वदेव\nप्राजापत्याः सर्वमित्यर्थवादः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Full of vigour and giving vigour, they are sacrifice, the womb of the immortal, and the world's support; on earth they are ever the source of wealth, and all belongs to the Prajapati's creatures': this is the explanatory praise."}},{"n":11,"text":"गावो ममैनः प्रणुदन्तु सौर्या-\nस्तथा सौम्याः स्वर्गयानाय सन्तु ।\nआम्नाता मे ददतीराश्रयं तु\nतथानुक्ताः सन्तु सर्वाशिषो मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"'May the cows of the sun wash away my sin, and the cows of the moon be for my journey to heaven. May those that are handed down give me refuge, and may all blessings, even unspoken, be mine.'"}},{"n":12,"text":"शेषोत्सर्गे कर्मभिर्देहमोक्षे\nसरस्वत्यः श्रेयसि संप्रवृत्ताः ।\nयूयं नित्यं पुण्यकर्मोपवाह्या\nदिशध्वं मे गतिमिष्टां प्रपन्नाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'When the rest is given up and the body released through deeds, you who flow like Sarasvati toward the good, bearers of merit always, grant me the goal I seek, for I have come to you.'"}},{"n":13,"text":"या वै यूयं सोऽहमद्यैकभावो\nयुष्मान्दत्त्वा चाहमात्मप्रदाता ।\nमनश्च्युता मनएवोपपन्नाः\nसंधुक्षध्वं सौम्यरूपोग्ररूपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'You are what I am; today I am one with you, and by giving you I give myself. Come from my mind into mind itself, and kindle me, whether gentle or fierce in form.'"}},{"n":14,"text":"एवं तस्याग्रे पूर्वमर्धं वदेत\nगवां दाता विधिवत्पूर्वदृष्टम् ।\nप्रतिब्रूयाच्छेषमर्धं द्विजातिः\nप्रतिगृह्णन्वै गोप्रदाने विधिज्ञः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the giver of cows should speak the first half in the presence of the cow as seen in the rule of old, and the brahmin who receives, knowing the rule, should answer with the other half."}},{"n":15,"text":"गां ददानीति वक्तव्यमर्घ्यवस्त्रवसुप्रदः ।\nऊधस्या भरितव्या च वैष्णवीति च चोदयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The giver, offering water of welcome, cloth and wealth, should say, 'I give a cow,' and urge that the udder be full and that she is Vishnu's."}},{"n":16,"text":"नाम संकीर्तयेत्तस्या यथासंख्योत्तरं स वै ।\nफलं षड्विंशदष्टौ च सहस्राणि च विंशतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should recite her name; the fruits in order are twenty-six, eight, and twenty thousand."}},{"n":17,"text":"एवमेतान्गुणान्वृद्धान्गवादीनां यथाक्रमम् ।\nगोप्रदाता समाप्नोति समस्तानष्टमे क्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way the giver of a cow gains in proper order these growing merits, with all of them complete at the eighth stage."}},{"n":18,"text":"गोदः शीली निर्भयश्चार्घदाता\nन स्याद्दुःखी वसुदाता च कामी ।\nऊधस्योढा भारत यश्च विद्वा-\nन्व्याख्यातास्ते वैष्णवाश्चन्द्रलोकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The giver of cows, the virtuous, the fearless, and the giver of water of welcome will not be unhappy; nor will the giver of wealth, nor one who is desirous. O Bharata, one who carries the full udder and is learned: these are said to reach Vishnu's moon-worlds."}},{"n":19,"text":"गा वै दत्त्वा गोव्रती स्यात्त्रिरात्रं\nनिशां चैकां संवसेतेह ताभिः ।\nकाम्याष्टम्यां वर्तितव्यं त्रिरात्रं\nरसैर्वा गोः शकृता प्रस्नवैर्वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given cows, one should keep the cow-vow for three nights and stay one night here with them. On the desired eighth day one should live three nights on the cows' milk products, dung, or urine."}},{"n":20,"text":"वेदव्रती स्याद्वृषभप्रदाता\nवेदावाप्तिर्गोयुगस्य प्रदाने ।\nतथा गवां विधिमासाद्य यज्वा\nलोकानग्र्यान्विन्दते नाविधिज्ञः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The giver of a bull should keep the Vedic vow; the giving of a pair of oxen brings knowledge of the Veda. So the sacrificer who has learned the rule about cows gains the highest worlds; one ignorant of the rule does not."}},{"n":21,"text":"कामान्सर्वान्पार्थिवानेकसंस्था-\nन्यो वै दद्यात्कामदुघां च धेनुम् ।\nसम्यक्ताः स्युर्हव्यकव्यौघवत्य-\nस्तासामुक्ष्णां ज्यायसां संप्रदानम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who, holding to one purpose, gives a wish-granting cow gains every earthly desire. Those cows rightly given are rich in offerings to gods and ancestors, and the best of bulls are to be given with them."}},{"n":22,"text":"न चाशिष्यायाव्रतायोपकुर्या-\nन्नाश्रद्दधानाय न वक्रबुद्धये ।\nगुह्यो ह्ययं सर्वलोकस्य धर्मो\nनेमं धर्मं यत्र तत्र प्रजल्पेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not do this for a non-disciple, one without vows, one without faith, or one of crooked mind. This is a secret dharma of all the world; one should not prattle of it anywhere."}},{"n":23,"text":"सन्ति लोके श्रद्दधाना मनुष्याः\nसन्ति क्षुद्रा राक्षसा मानुषेषु ।\nयेषां दानं दीयमानं ह्यनिष्टं\nनास्तिक्यं चाप्याश्रयन्ते ह्यपुण्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the world there are faithful people, and among men there are mean ones like demons, sinners who dislike a gift being given and take shelter in unbelief."}},{"n":24,"text":"बार्हस्पत्यं वाक्यमेतन्निशम्य\nये राजानो गोप्रदानानि कृत्वा ।\nलोकान्प्राप्ताः पुण्यशीलाः सुवृत्ता-\nस्तान्मे राजन्कीर्त्यमानान्निबोध ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, hear from me, as I name them, the kings who, having heard this word of Brihaspati and given cows, attained the worlds, virtuous and well-behaved."}},{"n":25,"text":"उशीनरो विष्वगश्वो नृगश्च\nभगीरथो विश्रुतो यौवनाश्वः ।\nमान्धाता वै मुचुकुन्दश्च राजा\nभूरिद्युम्नो नैषधः सोमकश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ushinara, Vishvagashva, Nriga, Bhagiratha, the renowned Yuvanashva, Mandhata, king Muchukunda, Bhuridyumna, the Nishadha king, and Somaka."}},{"n":26,"text":"पुरूरवा भरतश्चक्रवर्ती\nयस्यान्वये भारताः सर्व एव ।\nतथा वीरो दाशरथिश्च रामो\nये चाप्यन्ये विश्रुताः कीर्तिमन्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pururavas, and Bharata the universal emperor, in whose line all Bharatas stand; and the hero Rama, son of Dasharatha, and others who are famous and renowned."}},{"n":27,"text":"तथा राजा पृथुकर्मा दिलीपो\nदिवं प्राप्तो गोप्रदाने विधिज्ञः ।\nयज्ञैर्दानैस्तपसा राजधर्मै-\nर्मान्धाताभूद्गोप्रदानैश्च युक्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too king Dilipa, of great deeds, who knew the rule, reached heaven by giving cows. By sacrifices, gifts, austerity and kingly duties, and by cow-gifts, Mandhata became accomplished."}},{"n":28,"text":"तस्मात्पार्थ त्वमपीमां मयोक्तां\nबार्हस्पतीं भारतीं धारयस्व ।\nद्विजाग्र्येभ्यः संप्रयच्छ प्रतीतो\nगाः पुण्या वै प्राप्य राज्यं कुरूणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, son of Pritha, you too should keep this word of Brihaspati that I have told. Gladly give cows to the best brahmins, now that you have won the kingdom of the Kurus."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"तथा सर्वं कृतवान्धर्मराजो\nभीष्मेणोक्तो विधिवद्गोप्रदाने ।\nस मान्धातुर्देवदेवोपदिष्टं\nसम्यग्धर्मं धारयामास राजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of dharma did all this, as Bhishma instructed him in the rule for giving cows. The king properly held to the dharma taught to Mandhata by the god of gods."}},{"n":30,"text":"इति नृप सततं गवां प्रदाने\nयवशकलान्सह गोमयैः पिबानः ।\nक्षितितलशयनः शिखी यतात्मा\nवृष इव राजवृषस्तदा बभूव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, O king, constantly giving cows, drinking barley and dung, lying on the ground, with matted hair and self-controlled, he became then like a bull, a bull among kings."}},{"n":31,"text":"स नृपतिरभवत्सदैव ताभ्यः\nप्रयतमना ह्यभिसंस्तुवंश्च गा वै ।\nनृपधुरि च न गामयुङ्क्त भूय-\nस्तुरगवरैरगमच्च यत्र तत्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king always devoutly praised those cows with a focused mind. He no longer yoked cattle to the royal burden, but went wherever he wished with the finest horses."}}]}]}